Found by mcp-hub-worker during k144 (2026-11-06). Needs a decision before code.
Both HTTP transports report an HTTP error status by its reason phrase only, through _error_message($tx->error): "upstream NAME: Internal Server Error", "upstream NAME: Bad Request" -- no status code. Since k137 (Streamable HTTP) and k144 (HTTP+SSE) this is what an agent reads in the error result of its call, and what status/503 show for a failed start.
Question: should the status code be part of it ("upstream NAME: 500 Internal Server Error")? If yes, change both transports together (one helper for $tx->error), keep connection errors as they are ("Connection refused", "Request timeout"), and adjust the tests in t/http.t that match the text.

Decision by the main session (2026-11-10), under the maintainer's 'erledige die tickets von karr'; the maintainer may veto: yes. Both HTTP transports read an error status with its code ('upstream NAME: 500 Internal Server Error') through one helper; connection errors stay as they are; t/http.t follows.

Committed as 6e12488 (Read an HTTP error status with its code over both HTTP transports).
